{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":29059,"duration_api_ms":30038,"num_turns":10,"result":"I wrote `src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`, but I haven't run it. Running bpftrace needs root and I didn't check that it's installed. The `chmod +x` also needs your approval, so the file isn't executable yet.\n\nIt attaches to the `power:cpu_frequency` tracepoint. For each frequency change it prints the time in ms, the CPU, and the old and new frequency in MHz. It also keeps these maps:\n- **`@cur_mhz[cpu]`:** the latest frequency per CPU, printed every 5 seconds.\n- **`@transitions[cpu]`:** the number of frequency changes per CPU.\n- **`@freq_hist_mhz` and `@freq_by_cpu_mhz[cpu]`:** histograms of the frequencies seen, overall and per CPU. bpftrace prints these on Ctrl-C.\n\nThe \"old\" column shows 0 for a CPU's first change, because nothing has been recorded for it yet.\n\nRun it with `sudo bpftrace src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`. If no events appear, your cpufreq driver may not emit that tracepoint. This can happen on VMs and with some governors.\n\nI put it in a new `49-cpufreq` directory to follow the numbering. Tell me if you'd rather have a different location, or a README to go with it.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"46d6037e-b110-4fe3-b944-3f5c7c5db41d","total_cost_usd":0.115036,"usage":{"input_tokens":18,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3270,"cache_read_input_tokens":211345,"output_tokens":2591,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3270},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":465,"cache_read_input_tokens":28417,"cache_creation_input_tokens":131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":131,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":351,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000451,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":2591,"cacheReadInputTokens":211345,"cacheCreationInputTokens":3270,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.11458499999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01BZe1yBNQvaftCw5B7emLFS","tool_input":{"command":"ls src | grep -i -E \"cpu|freq\"; find . -name \"*.bt\" -not -path \"./src/third_party/*\" | head; which bpftrace; ls /sys/kernel/tracing/events/power 2>/dev/null | head -20"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wbi4fizhf8csqPV9tv3zbL","tool_input":{"command":"cd src/49-cpufreq && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='cpufreq.bt'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"(nsecs - @start) / 1000000\",\"elapsed / 1000000\")\ns=s.replace(\"\\nEND\\n{\\n    clear(@start);\\n}\\n\",\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nchmod +x cpufreq.bt; which bpftrace && ls /sys/kernel/tracing/events/power/cpu_frequency 2>&1 | head -3; tail -15 cpufreq.bt"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SzpGvQjgdq7GkNMyjwNJom","tool_input":{"command":"chmod +x src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt; which bpftrace"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ccccde81-269f-4a84-acf6-72d532dd102a"}

